  "term": "gangliosidosis",
  "definition": "Gangliosidosis is a group of inherited lysosomal storage disorders in which gangliosides build up because the enzymes or helper factors needed to break them down in lysosomes do not work properly. These disorders are grouped according to which ganglioside accumulates.",
